WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
A headline: students sleep
seven point one hours a night,

2
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.910
plus or minus nought point two,
ninety-five per cent confidence.

3
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.330
A second survey of different students
gets a mean of seven point two eight.

4
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.380
A third survey gets six point nine two.

5
00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:18.440
So what does that plus or minus promise?

6
00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.670
That most students sleep in that range?

7
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.130
That the truth is surely inside it?

8
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.350
In this mission, you'll see
that a sample mean varies,

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.310
and is an unbiased estimate
of the population mean, mu.

10
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.970
You'll find that sample means
spread less than single values:

11
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.560
variance sigma squared over n.

12
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.330
And you'll build an interval: an estimate,

13
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.300
plus or minus a margin.

14
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.950
Your mission: explain what the plus
or minus in the sleep survey promises.
